---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Layerwatch"
  description="How Layerwatch collects, uses, and protects your information."
>

  <!-- Header -->
  <div class="fixed top-4 sm:top-6 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 z-50 w-[calc(100%-2rem)] max-w-6xl">
    <header class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 sm:px-7 h-16 rounded-2xl border border-border-subtle bg-surface/70 backdrop-blur-md shadow-[0_8px_30px_rgba(0,0,0,0.35)]">
      <a href="/"><img src="/logo-header.png" alt="Layerwatch" class="h-14 w-auto" /></a>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/layerwatch"
        class="hidden sm:inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-text-muted text-sm hover:text-white transition-colors"
      >
        <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M12 .5C5.73.5.75 5.48.75 11.75c0 5.02 3.26 9.28 7.77 10.78.57.1.78-.25.78-.55 0-.27-.01-1.16-.02-2.1-3.16.69-3.83-1.34-3.83-1.34-.52-1.31-1.26-1.66-1.26-1.66-1.03-.7.08-.69.08-.69 1.14.08 1.74 1.17 1.74 1.17 1.01 1.73 2.65 1.23 3.3.94.1-.73.4-1.23.72-1.51-2.52-.29-5.17-1.26-5.17-5.6 0-1.24.44-2.25 1.17-3.04-.12-.29-.51-1.45.11-3.02 0 0 .96-.31 3.14 1.16a10.9 10.9 0 0 1 5.72 0c2.18-1.47 3.14-1.16 3.14-1.16.62 1.57.23 2.73.11 3.02.73.79 1.17 1.8 1.17 3.04 0 4.35-2.66 5.31-5.19 5.59.41.35.77 1.04.77 2.1 0 1.52-.01 2.74-.01 3.11 0 .3.2.66.79.55A11.26 11.26 0 0 0 23.25 11.75C23.25 5.48 18.27.5 12 .5Z"/></svg>
        GitHub
      </a>
    </header>
  </div>

  <main class="relative px-6 pt-40 pb-28 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <span class="eyebrow mb-4">Legal</span>
    <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mt-4 mb-3">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-text-muted/60 text-sm mb-14 font-mono">Effective August 21, 2026</p>

    <div class="legal-content space-y-10 text-text-muted leading-relaxed">

      <section>
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>
          This policy covers <strong class="text-white">layerwatch.dev</strong> and the free tools we publish
          (the browser extension, and the open-source MCP proxy once released). It explains what we collect,
          why, and how you can control it. The short version: we collect as little as possible, and we never
          sell your data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Information we collect</h2>
        <p>We collect information in two ways:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">Waitlist signups.</strong> When you submit your email through the early
            access form on this site, it's sent to and stored by our form provider, Formspree, so we can
            notify you about access and product updates.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">Automatic connection logs.</strong> Like most websites, requests to
            layerwatch.dev pass through our hosting provider, Cloudflare, which logs standard technical data
            (IP address, browser type, request timestamps) for security and performance. We don't run our own
            analytics or tracking scripts on this site.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How we use your information</h2>
        <p>
          We use your email solely to reach out about early access and material product updates. We do not
          sell, rent, or share your information with third parties for marketing purposes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Third-party services</h2>
        <p>We rely on a small number of infrastructure providers to run this site:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Formspree</strong> — processes waitlist form submissions.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Cloudflare</strong> — hosting, CDN, and security.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Each operates under its own privacy policy governing the data it processes on our behalf.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          layerwatch.dev does not set its own tracking or advertising cookies. Cloudflare may set minimal,
          essential cookies required for security and site performance.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Data retention</h2>
        <p>
          We retain your email address for as long as you remain on the waitlist. You can request removal at
          any time — see Contact below.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          You can request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal data at any time by
          contacting us. We will respond within a reasonable timeframe.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Our services are not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect information from anyone
          under the age of 16.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Our products</h2>
        <p>
          The Layerwatch browser extension processes everything locally in your browser — it has no
          background service worker and makes no network requests. Read the full
          <a href="https://github.com/layerwatch/browser-extension/blob/main/PRIVACY_POLICY.md">extension privacy policy</a>
          for details. The MCP proxy, when released, will run entirely on your own machine and write logs only
          to your local filesystem — nothing is sent to Layerwatch.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If this policy changes, we'll update the effective date above and, for material changes, notify the
          waitlist by email.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy or your data? Email
          <a href="mailto:hi@layerwatch.dev">hi@layerwatch.dev</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <footer class="relative border-t border-border-subtle px-6 pt-16 pb-8 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute top-0 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 w-full max-w-3xl h-px bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-primary/40 to-transparent"></div>

    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto relative z-10">
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-6 pb-12">
        <a href="/"><img src="/logo-header.png" alt="Layerwatch" class="h-10 w-auto self-start" /></a>

        <div class="flex items-center gap-6">
          <p class="text-text-muted/50 text-xs uppercase tracking-widest font-mono">Connect</p>
          <ul class="flex items-center gap-6 text-sm">
            <li><a href="https://github.com/layerwatch" class="text-text-muted hover:text-white transition-colors">GitHub</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://x.com/layerwatch" class="text-text-muted hover:text-white transition-colors">X</a></li>
            <li><a href="mailto:hi@layerwatch.dev" class="text-text-muted hover:text-white transition-colors">Contact</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pt-6 border-t border-border-subtle flex flex-col sm:flex-row justify-between gap-2">
        <p class="text-text-muted/60 text-xs">© 2026 Layerwatch. All rights reserved.</p>
        <div class="flex gap-4">
          <a href="/privacy" class="text-text-muted/60 hover:text-white text-xs transition-colors">Privacy</a>
          <a href="/terms" class="text-text-muted/60 hover:text-white text-xs transition-colors">Terms</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>

</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-content h2 {
    color: white;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .legal-content p { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .legal-content ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .legal-content a {
    color: var(--color-primary-light);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .legal-content a:hover { color: white; }
</style>
